@startuml overview
' cumin-works - handing an issue back to its Assignee for a decision.
' A state is a label on GitHub, written without "cumin/status/". "do /" says who works in the state.
' A gray state belongs to another area.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "a state in work" as Work #EEEEEE
Work : (planning, implementing, checking,\nreviewing, merging, accepting)

state "awaiting-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Assignee reads the comment,\nchooses, and writes the decision

state "ready" as Ready #EEEEEE
Ready : (each area decides what comes next)

Work --> Decision : stop\n[the agent asked, or cumin stopped the work]\n/ the comment has the reason, the choices,\nand what the Assignee does for each\n/ cumin notifies
Decision --> Ready : the Assignee adds ready

@enduml
